`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Source inspection on 2026-10-18: Blender ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"v4.5.0"})," resolves to ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"8cb6b388974a817afedf1317ce26f0c75aa5f181"}),"; Godot ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"4.5-stable"})," is the existing ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d"})," pin. These are selected source versions, not installed builds. No bake, GPU job, image save, failure or reopen fixture was executed. Blender manual/API retrieval was unavailable during this check; the Blender claims below use inspected implementation and RNA definitions."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"blender-target-mutation-is-separate-from-image-delivery",children:"Blender: target mutation is separate from image delivery"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The RNA target definitions distinguish image data-blocks associated with active material image-texture nodes from active mesh color attributes. The image-target validation checks UV presence and image initialization. A material slot without an active image can produce an informational report and continue, so the intended target inventory needs its own check; do not infer every material received a result from one operator status. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/blender/blender/blob/8cb6b388974a817afedf1317ce26f0c75aa5f181/source/blender/makesrna/intern/rna_scene.cc#L432-L453",children:"Target definitions"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/blender/blender/blob/8cb6b388974a817afedf1317ce26f0c75aa5f181/source/blender/editors/object/object_bake_api.cc",children:"validation, lines 499–589"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The operator exposes an external filepath and save-mode enum, but the inspected initialization explicitly rewrites EXTERNAL to INTERNAL. Thus supplying a filepath does not establish a written texture in this version. Image output is marked dirty. An explicit ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"Image.save"})," path reports save failures; ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"Image.pack"})," can package dirty image data in memory. Packing alone does not save the containing ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:".blend"})," to disk. These are available persistence routes, not a claim that every alternative is invalid. Retain output reports, saved bytes and a cold-reopen observation rather than accepting an in-memory preview. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/blender/blender/blob/8cb6b388974a817afedf1317ce26f0c75aa5f181/source/blender/makesrna/intern/rna_scene.cc#L432-L453",children:"Advertised modes, lines 446–453"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/blender/blender/blob/8cb6b388974a817afedf1317ce26f0c75aa5f181/source/blender/editors/object/object_bake_api.cc",children:"forced mode, lines 1918–1922; filepath, 2253–2257; dirty image, 331"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/blender/blender/blob/8cb6b388974a817afedf1317ce26f0c75aa5f181/source/blender/makesrna/intern/rna_image_api.cc",children:"image save/pack, lines 91–145 and 303–329"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The invoke path, when no bake job is already running, launches a job and returns RUNNING_MODAL; an existing bake job instead returns CANCELLED. The modal handler reports FINISHED once that job no longer exists; this condition alone does not distinguish successful baking from cancellation or failure. The synchronous execution path returns a bake result, but its non-selected-to-active batch loop assigns the result repeatedly and returns the last value. ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Adapter implication:"})," record dispatch mode, target/object inventory, per-object reports, output changes and persistence independently. No failed-batch or cancellation behavior was reproduced. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/blender/blender/blob/8cb6b388974a817afedf1317ce26f0c75aa5f181/source/blender/editors/object/object_bake_api.cc",children:"Invocation, lines 2171–2220; modal, 139–151; synchronous path, 1931–1989"})]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"godot-native-editor-operation-atlas-resources-and-scene-identities",children:"Godot: native editor operation, atlas resources and scene identities"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The inspected stock script binding leaves ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"LightmapGI::bake"})," commented out. The editor plugin calls that native method, choosing the edited root or the lightmap's parent as the scan root. This establishes an editor/native path, not a callable GDScript bake method or an implemented GameMap adapter. Custom native integrations are not ruled out. The pinned class documentation says exported projects cannot bake lightmaps and qualifies the Forward+/Mobile-capable-device requirement with “if no custom lightmappers are installed.” Rendering already baked lightmaps is a separate capability. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/3d/lightmap_gi.cpp",children:"Binding, line 1893"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/editor/scene/3d/lightmap_gi_editor_plugin.cpp",children:"editor dispatch, lines 39–78"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/doc/classes/LightmapGI.xml",children:"class scope, lines 7–13"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["For ordinary MeshInstance3D collection, the source requires visible Static-GI meshes and triangle surfaces with UV2 and normals, and records transforms relative to the LightmapGI. Native bake rejects a missing save path, missing eligible meshes or a computed lightmap dimension of zero. A ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"(0,0)"})," mesh size hint receives a 64×64 fallback before scaling. The versioned tutorial additionally warns that hiding a Light does not remove its contribution: use its Disabled bake mode. Fully baked static-surface lighting does not update merely because a light is moved or recolored. UV2/import state and bake generation therefore belong in the evidence record. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/3d/lightmap_gi.cpp",children:"Collection, lines 373–415; initial gates, 885–951"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/tutorials/3d/global_illumination/using_lightmap_gi.html",children:"4.5 workflow and light modes"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The native save path writes EXR lightmap atlases and optional PNG shadowmask atlases plus import configuration, reimports them, and requires loaded texture resources. It then records each baked user's NodePath, atlas UV scale, slice and sub-instance index in LightmapGIData, saves that resource, and assigns it to the live node. Later assignment resolves the paths and warns when previously baked nodes are missing. Image files alone do not establish that the current scene uses the intended bake. The inspected editor functions do not save a PackedScene as part of this operation. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/3d/lightmap_gi.cpp",children:"Atlas persistence, lines 808–882; user associations, 1322–1333; final save/assignment, 1469–1479; path resolution, 1510–1543"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Two completion/recovery boundaries matter. First, the editor calls its end-of-bake routine before inspecting the returned error; that routine prints “Done baking lightmaps” regardless of that result. Second, the native path saves atlas files, then detaches and clears existing LightmapGIData before its final resource save. A later save error returns before reassigning it. These source paths do not establish atomic replacement or rollback, and no corruption was observed. Keep a recoverable previous generation and validate artifacts, native result, scene association and fresh reopen separately. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/editor/scene/3d/lightmap_gi_editor_plugin.cpp",children:"Editor completion/error ordering, lines 69–124 and 163–174"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/3d/lightmap_gi.cpp",children:"replacement ordering, lines 1281–1308 and 1469–1479"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Documentation discrepancy to preserve:"})," the pinned LightmapGI class note says PrimitiveMesh cannot bake because it cannot store UV2, while the versioned 4.5 tutorial describes primitive Add UV2 support. The tutorial separately provides a CSG-to-MeshInstance conversion route; that workaround changes representation and is not itself a contradiction of unsupported direct CSG baking. Do not turn the broad PrimitiveMesh statement into an unconditional eligibility rule. Inspect the actual generated mesh, UV2, normals, size hints and selected build; the conversion/import/reopen fixture remains unrun. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/doc/classes/LightmapGI.xml",children:"Class note"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/tutorials/3d/global_illumination/using_lightmap_gi.html",children:"primitive/CSG workflows"})]}),`
