`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Use a small rights-cleared room, an emissive surface, a static light, a dynamic light and an intentionally excluded object. Freeze geometry/material/light transforms, UV layers, engine and renderer, bake settings, color/exposure interpretation, source revision, scene generation and intended receiver inventory."}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"For Blender, record exact active image/color targets, pass/filter and selected-to-active settings. Compare the image buffer, explicit saved texture or packed-and-saved project, and cold-reopened data. Include a missing material target and a canceled operation; neither a status string nor a changed preview certifies every output."}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"For Godot, retain atlas/import/resource hashes and per-node UV/slice associations. Save the project-owned scene after the bake through a separately verified route, reopen in a fresh process and compare a fixed camera under recorded display settings. Test a missing UV2 receiver, renamed/reparented baked node, hidden versus Disabled light, and geometry/light changes without rebaking. Treat changed source inputs as a stale-generation condition even when old lighting still looks plausible. Exercise interrupted or failed saves only in disposable copies; keep previous artifacts rather than overwriting the sole recoverable baseline."}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Accept terminal success, artifact integrity, current scene association, persistence and rendered appearance as separate gates. Seam/noise/leakage tolerances, GPU/device compatibility, cancellation recovery, crash durability and actual target-build behavior need runtime evidence; the sources do not supply those results."}),`
