`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Godot's ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_audioeffectcapture.html",children:"AudioEffectCapture reference"})," describes raw frames copied from its attached audio bus into a ring buffer. Its ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"get_buffer(n)"})," returns the requested count or an empty array when insufficient frames are available. Empty reads are not evidence of silent samples. The capture does not encode a finished audio asset."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The pinned ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/servers/audio_server.cpp#L538-L657",children:"AudioServer mixing path"})," processes enabled effects in sequence before applying that bus's volume and mute/solo attenuation, then sends the result downstream. ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Source-derived implication:"})," a capture effect can contain nonzero input while its own bus is muted. Moving it around an effect chain changes the observed processing stage. A child-bus capture does not automatically include downstream processing or other buses. Even a last effect on Master precedes Master bus gain/mute in this implementation."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/tutorials/audio/audio_buses.html",children:"audio-bus guide"})," is marked not yet updated for 4.5 and warns that Web Sample playback does not support these effects; Stream playback is required, with a latency tradeoff when threads are unavailable. The ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/tutorials/export/exporting_for_web.html#audio-playback",children:"versioned Web-export guide"})," independently documents the same Sample/Stream limitation without that stale-page banner. Record playback mode rather than treating an unsupported observation route as silence. Keep the initial fixture stereo; surround coverage and channel-pair ownership need separate validation."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"2-distinguish-observation-loss-from-playback-failure",children:"2. Distinguish observation loss from playback failure"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The pinned ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/servers/audio/effects/audio_effect_capture.cpp#L121-L140",children:"capture implementation"})," copies input to output regardless of ring capacity. It inserts the incoming processing block only when the ring has enough space for the entire block; otherwise it increments ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"discarded_frames"})," by that block's frame count. Thus capture loss does not, by itself, prove an audible engine underrun."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/servers/audio/effects/audio_effect_capture.cpp#L34-L119",children:"same implementation's buffer methods"})," show that ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"clear_buffer()"})," advances the read position without resetting pushed/discarded counters. The public reference says buffer-length changes have no effect after initialization. Use counter baselines/deltas and actual reported frame capacity; do not assume that setting a larger duration repaired the current capture. A clear is an explicit observation discontinuity even when the overflow counter stays unchanged. Counter totals alone do not locate each missing interval precisely."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"3-separate-rendered-buffers-export-completion-and-audible-output",children:"3. Separate rendered buffers, export completion and audible output"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Unreal's ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/audio-mixer-overview-in-unreal-engine?application_version=5.5",children:"5.5 mixer overview"})," describes submix output as a combination of child submixes and registered/sent sources, processed through the submix effect chain. It separately describes rendering future buffers ahead of the buffer currently heard. Capture therefore establishes a selected render-path observation, not physical speaker output."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/API/Runtime/Engine/ISubmixBufferListener?application_version=5.5",children:"ISubmixBufferListener"})," receives a newly rendered submix buffer with owning submix, sample/channel counts, sample rate and ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"AudioClock"}),". Preserve those fields; the inspected reference does not establish a shared clock epoch with game ticks, video timestamps or device presentation, nor a precise pre/post-gain placement for every listener path. Do not manufacture that alignment from parameter names."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/python-api/class/AudioMixerLibrary?application_version=5.5",children:"AudioMixerLibrary"})," distinguishes pause from finalization and defaults a missing submix selection to master output. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/python-api/class/SoundSubmix?application_version=5.5",children:"SoundSubmix"})," exposes ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"on_submix_recorded_file_done"})," for completed file export. Keep stop intent, export notification, independently reopened artifact and acoustic observation as separate outcomes. These pages do not establish cancellation, crash-safe durability or safe overlapping recording requests."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Godot's ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_audioserver.html",children:"AudioServer reference"})," identifies driver-dependent output latency and warns against querying it every frame. Headless selects the Dummy driver. Its ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/tutorials/audio/sync_with_audio.html",children:"synchronization tutorial"}),", explicitly marked not yet updated for 4.5, discusses chunked playback position, latency correction, jitter and hardware/system-clock drift. Treat these as estimation guidance, not measured device latency or proof of synchronization."]}),`
