`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Browser-engine observation and export also have separate completion surfaces: ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://threejs.org/docs/pages/WebGLRenderer",children:"Three.js asynchronous render-target readback"})," resolves pixel data, while ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://threejs.org/docs/pages/GLTFExporter.html",children:"GLTFExporter.parseAsync"})," resolves exported data and requires renderer-specific utilities for compressed textures. Neither promise alone saves an evidence file or proves downstream importer fidelity. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/BabylonJS/Documentation/blob/master/content/setup/support/serverSide.md",children:"Babylon NullEngine"})," requires no WebGL device but produces no rendering; server/test/import support under it cannot establish visual correctness. Cancellation, idempotent retry and output durability remain unverified."]}),`
