`,e.jsx(e.Fragment,{children:e.jsx(n.pre,{className:"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark",style:{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},tabIndex:"0",icon:'<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M 6,1 C 4.354992,1 3,2.354992 3,4 v 16 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 12 c 1.645008,0 3,-1.354992 3,-3 V 8 7 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 20.707031,6.2929687 l -5,-5 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 15,1 h -1 z m 0,2 h 7 v 3 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 3 v 11 c 0,0.564129 -0.435871,1 -1,1 H 6 C 5.4358712,21 5,20.564129 5,20 V 4 C 5,3.4358712 5.4358712,3 6,3 Z M 15,3.4140625 18.585937,7 H 16 C 15.435871,7 15,6.5641288 15,6 Z" fill="currentColor" /></svg>',children:e.jsx(n.code,{children:e.jsx(n.span,{className:"line",children:e.jsx(n.span,{children:"rhubarb --machineReadable --recognizer pocketSphinx --exportFormat json --extendedShapes GHX --dialogFile line.txt --output line.cues.candidate.json line.wav"})})})})}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"The input is last. Default recognizer is pocketSphinx, default export is TSV; JSON must be selected. --output overwrites an existing destination; omit it and results go to stdout. Use a fresh candidate path, separate from source audio and accepted cues. (sources R4, R5)"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The pinned file factory selects .wav or .ogg case-insensitively, rejecting other extensions. WAV decoding expects little-endian RIFF/WAVE and uncompressed PCM or IEEE float, including supported extensible subformats: ordinary 8/16/24/32-bit PCM and 32/64-bit float are covered by the reader; it rejects unsupported codec/sample organization. .ogg means Ogg ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Vorbis"}),", not every codec in an Ogg container. Both readers average channels into mono. Recognition resamples segments internally to 16 kHz and a 16-bit buffer: “input must already be 16-kHz mono PCM” would be incorrect. Source does not establish a general maximum file length or universal decoder robustness. A clean single-speaker mono delivery file is a proposed fixture choice, not a CLI requirement. Multichannel averaging can cancel opposite-polarity speech or mix speakers, so validate the actual analysis signal. (sources R6–R8)"]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["pocketSphinx is intended for English; --dialogFile supplies ASCII/UTF-8 text to bias its word model rather than forcing an exact transcript. The source combines ordinary and dialogue-biased language models, then aligns recognized words’ phones. phonetic is documented for non-English/language-independent use, with lower typical precision; the pinned implementation still uses the packaged acoustic/phone models and ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"ignores dialogue for recognition"})," (the CLI still reads a supplied --dialogFile). Do not promise text-assisted non-English alignment. (sources R4, R7, R9)"]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"cue-semantics-and-completion",children:"Cue semantics and completion"}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"JSON contains metadata.soundFile (absolute source path), metadata.duration, and mouthCues entries with start, end and value. Times are seconds relative to the recording. Internally the timeline is integer centiseconds; duration is truncated downward to a 0.01-second boundary. This is not sample accuracy, game-frame timing, subtitle text or a confidence score. Adjacent intervals share boundaries. The JSON exporter also emits a zero-length idle fallback when animation is empty, so mere nonempty mouthCues does not establish usable speech. (sources R10)"}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Labels are A–F plus selected G/H/X: A closes lips; B slightly open with clenched teeth; C open; D wide-open; E rounded; F puckered; G lower-lip/upper-teeth; H tongue-up; X rest. A–F are mandatory in the tool’s target shape set; --extendedShapes defaults to GHX and an empty string disables all three. These are animation categories, not engine blend-shape names or one-to-one phoneme IDs. The animation pipeline applies timing optimization, pauses, tween insertion and shape-set conversion after recognition. A cue boundary therefore need not equal a raw phoneme boundary. (sources R4, R11)"}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"--machineReadable emits newline-delimited JSON status on stderr: start, progress, success, failure (with reason), and log. Preserve unknown event types/fields rather than failing future-compatible input. Source caveats:"}),`
