`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Use actual process termination + expected success status for a generation invocation + independently reopened/parsed artifact. Retain stderr and exit/signal outcome. Progress 1.0 is not completion. No resumable/cancellation/atomic replacement contract was established; a killed process or missing terminal event is an uncertain/failed candidate, never an accepted asset. (sources R5, R12)"}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"project-owned-mapping-and-one-engine-interface",children:"Project-owned mapping and one engine interface"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Proposed GameMap adapter, unimplemented:"})," version a map from every enabled cue label to project-owned sprite frame/attachment, rig pose, or blend-weight vector. Require asset/mesh identity, explicit neutral pose and transition policy; reject unmapped labels instead of guessing an ARKit/other naming convention. Map seconds using the actual audio instance and seek/playback position, with declared lead/lag and latency treatment. Treat pause, resume, pitch/rate change, seek, loop, skip and stop as clock/state transitions. On restart invalidate the old dialogue/audio epoch; recompute the current shape after seek rather than replaying stale cue events. The <0.01-second truncated tail requires a declared end/neutral policy. No universal sample-to-game-clock alignment is supplied by Rhubarb."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["One official engine API usable by a custom consumer is ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Godot 4.5 MeshInstance3D"}),": find_blend_shape_by_name returns -1 when absent (including null mesh), set_blend_shape_value applies a weight at a valid index, and get_blend_shape_value reads it. An invalid get can return 0.0 with an error, so zero alone is not a successful neutral-pose check. Resolve and validate names against the particular mesh before writing/reading. This is an engine API building block, ",e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"not an official Rhubarb integration"})," or proof that weights look correct or remain in sync. Existing GameMap audio-clock/capture contracts still apply. (sources R13)"]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"acceptance-fixture-and-rights",children:"Acceptance fixture and rights"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Unimplemented acceptance proposal:"})," archive tool/build/resource identity, recognizer/options, input hash, source audio duration/rate/channels, transcript hash where used, cue bytes, mapping version, engine/importer identity and audio-instance/session epoch. Validate finite sorted contiguous cue intervals within the truncated duration, enabled labels, positive usable clip length and matching source identity; bind by content hash rather than metadata path alone. Preserve the original output when stripping a private absolute path for distribution."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Use owned short recordings with speech onsets/closures, pauses and a non-centisecond end; include silence/sub-10-ms input, wrong-language/script conditions, stereo phase cancellation, absent models, bad input and interrupted output. In a disposable consuming scene inspect actual mapped shapes alongside captured audio/video through pause/seek/restart and locale/audio replacement. Keep three outcomes separate: structurally accepted cue artifact, correct mapping/playback clock behavior, and human/perceptual lip-sync quality. No measured recognition accuracy, latency, repeatability or perceptual quality was established."}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"The pinned LICENSE identifies Rhubarb itself as MIT and supplies separate third-party notices, including the CMU Sphinx US-English acoustic model’s BSD terms. Its nonbinding summary says generated lip-sync data belongs to the user and distinguishes production-only use from shipping lip-sync functionality. Retain applicable notices when redistributing software/resources; none of this clears the recording, performer, voice-clone or project-art rights. (sources R14)"}),`
