`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"For prerecorded browser-game cinematics, attach timed text to an HTML video element and check cue delivery. Engine-native dialogue, Web Audio, and canvas scenes need their own subtitle integrations."}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Source pins."})," WebVTT ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/CRD-webvtt1-20260520/",children:"Candidate Recommendation Draft, 2026-05-20"})," remains a work in progress. HTML was source-inspected at ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66/source",children:"de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66"}),", dated 2026-10-16. These are specification pins, not browser-implementation or compatibility results."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Artifact and identity."})," WebVTT uses UTF-8 text and millisecond-formatted timestamps; cue starts are nondecreasing and each end must exceed its start. Caption/subtitle intervals may overlap. Identifiers are optional, but this draft requires supplied identifiers to be unique within the file. The parser can discard a malformed timing block while successfully processing the file; even a signature-only file can successfully produce zero cues. Consequently, syntax conformance and expected cue inventory require separate checks. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/CRD-webvtt1-20260520/#file-structure",children:"File syntax"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/CRD-webvtt1-20260520/#file-parsing",children:"parser"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Native consumer."})," A child track supplies src, kind, srclang and label; subtitles require srclang. Hidden mode maintains active cues without displaying them; showing overlays captions/subtitles; disabled does not initiate obtaining cues, has no active cues and suppresses cue events. Switching to disabled is not an unconditional cancellation of an in-flight fetch or deletion of already-loaded cues. HTMLTrackElement.readyState distinguishes NONE, LOADING, LOADED and ERROR. Load follows parsing; network/CORS and fatal format-processing failures produce error. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66/source#L37936-L38206",children:"Track"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66/source#L42310-L42395",children:"modes"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66/source#L42930-L43089",children:"loading"})]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Clock and reset."})," Active membership uses media time with start <= time < end. Seeking recomputes membership; cues skipped by a seek are not classified as missed playback cues. Slow processing can omit short cues from activeCues. Setting, changing or removing track src immediately empties its cue list. getCueById returns the first matching cue. These events are not a rendered-pixel receipt. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66/source#L41361-L41528",children:"Activation"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66/source#L43085-L43090",children:"reset"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/de953a7cf0523f5873a1904ba2ce010c689dfb66/source#L43542-L43571",children:"lookup"})]}),`
